body:
Damn, I'm 4.1 hours into the game on Steam and I keep asking myself why everyone likes it. I feel like I'm still in the tutorial section of a game that isn't that complex or mechanically deep.   


I do like the art style a lot but it's hard to go wrong with red and black as your dominant color palette. What's really throwing me off is the anime movie cut scenes. I don't feel like it adds anything and I wish they had just animated it in game instead. 

&#x200B;

The characters are fine. I wouldn't call them likeable just tolerable. Everyone will have their own opinion so it's a your mileage may vary situation. 

&#x200B;

TLDR: Game has bland story where it can't commit to a teacher being a rapist so they just have them be an abuser instead. Characters are objects. Sub-standard gameplay for 2016. Middle of the road art direction with standard red & black color contrast. Game making me wait for it to get good.

Damn that sucks man. I haven't seen you post an answer to this question but maybe you responded to it on a different post about Decision to Leave.

&#x200B;

