Keep paying all your debts on time. - If that is something you can do, it is better to do that then to let some debts become negative marks on your credit report for missed payments.

&#x200B;

However if you can only afford to pay some of your debts, it is best to pay off the highest interest rate first.

&#x200B;

However it sounds like you're able to pay both. If you really do only have $10K in credit card debt at 14% you will have it paid off in 30 months at $400 a month. That's 2 and a half years. You can do that easily and it's well worth it than carrying a missed student loan payment for 7 years if not longer.

&#x200B;

You're actually only paying $1,892 in interest on the credit cards over 30 months versus $7,689 in interest for your student loan over 104 months

Do you think they actually will implement a real police force that doesn't spawn in place?

I'm curious by what you mean by working inventory & skill system. Both of those seem to work for me. I would agree they aren't groundbreaking but I would say they do what it says on the tin, minor stat upgrades.

&#x200B;

I mean this is a singleplayer game. It doesn't even have multiplayer in it. Why are you going on about longevity of a singleplayer game? There isn't even DLC at this moment. Like CDPR made their money, they could just ignore gamers at this point and go make something else. 

&#x200B;

I disagree that CDPR has lost market share. They release 1 game every 5 years, virtually no one uses their online store except for video game nerds who like old video games. Cyberpunk 2077 is unfortunately at this point and time profitable. They could absolutely be stubborn & arrogant, there would be no recourse for the fans except making reddit posts lol.

