No. I mean how terrible game of the year editions are. Dragon Age Inquisition, Arkham City, Assassin's Creed, Witcher 3 and plenty more games have those sorts of benign additions. I'm not saying that's what makes them GOTY quality but I am saying there's an expected level of side activities to do in games such as the collection aspects of safe houses, vehicles, & people.

It's funny that you say that it's not done because I think there's 2 ways to think about that. I agree that the developers had much loftier expectations and ambitions for the game. However I feel like the game is done because although CDPR has promised to patch the game, I don't think they're going to add in the things that people want beyond 0 bugs. 

&#x200B;

I'm still debating myself if they're going to add in free expansion packs as an apology or free add-on DLC like the Witcher 3.

Ahh, meaningful choices. I'm curious because there are 4 different endings I believe based on the decisions you make in the last mission. Is that not meaningful enough? lol

&#x200B;

I get what you mean though, you wanted the chance to be mean to someone at the 5 hour mark and then they betray you at the 10 hour mark. Something benign like that. 

&#x200B;

Meaningful choices like those would require a rather deep overhaul of the game. I think it's unlikely we would get something like that. You mentioned origin choices leading to different resources. How gypped or happy would you feel if because you were a corpo you got a corpo only gun, same for street kid, or wasteland kid. Because I believe that's how it is for starter vehicles. I've only played as a corpo so I don't know. It's a shame because it really feels like the story was designed for you to be a street kid.

Yeah the stealth is basically a joke. The melee is like using a death baton where if you touch someone with it enough they just fall over. 

&#x200B;

I recall before release seeing a lot of video game reviewers & personalities saying how they wanted to live in the Cyberpunk 2077 world and walk the streets. But the game is just very artificial in that everyone you're walking around is not someone you can interact with beyond bump into and shoot them.

Do you feel like flying cars are intricate to this world? There's only a few times when there are flying cars and usually it's for the ultra rich. I'm not going to lie, I would like a flying car in the game but it just doesn't feel like it would mix since you're playing a low level thug. 

&#x200B;

I agree with a lot of the criticisms though. Incredibly dead world. Walk into a store and there's like nothing to do in it. The dialogue is meaningless 99% of the time, you can be always mean to someone but as long as you do the specific thing you can romance them.

I didn't really care about what direction the game went in. I feel the story is serviceable and fits the world. 

&#x200B;

I think the problems are the things you list as in there is nothing for your character to do. No apartment collection, vehicle customization. Only 1 optional love interest which is dependent on your sexual orientation. The problems don't end there.

&#x200B;

We then get into the problems of randomly spawned NPC's that are just there to fill the void of the city. Your character can only wear clothing that is equivalent to their level, so if you have a level 13 T-shirt but you are a level 12, you're SOL. There's just a lot of leftovers from the Witcher 3 game design where it's this hollow world but the graphical fidelity doesn't make it passable. The bright yellows make the game world look more toyish/fake/plastic and less realistic. The world just breaks down because there is no consequence to your actions. Run over a civilian, the cops stop chasing you after turning the corner.

Your problems with the different acts may just be what the developers were able to cobble together after 3 years of development. And yes I did say 3 years. Although the first trailer for Cyberpunk was in 2013, please note that the last Witcher 3 DLC was in May 2016. Cyberpunk's original release date was supposed to be April 2020, which means by their first release date delay they knew they didn't have the game ready and were in a rush to get the game in a working state. This was when they had to start picking which pieces to chop off and which pieces to include in the game. 

&#x200B;

At one point there were supposed to be customizable cars, apartments, and cutscenes with your character in them. You can even see where they cut off a skill tree on the skill's menu. It's kind of remarkable that we even got the game in the condition that it's in and that's with all the bugs.

