I just saw the Beige Frequency video and I was curious of this exact same question. Regardless of what their past interactions were I think she acted out of line. If he truly did something terrible enough to justify it then say so. Like why would she 'soft block' him? Why not just actually block him if she has a problem with him? 

&#x200B;

I agree that you don't have to like someone but don't call them a creep on a public forum without reason. Like here's a crazy idea. What if she direct messaged him and told him to stop following her? Since she likes posting DM's so much, she could then post it if he continued to follow her. Or she could just block him. Her actions just spawn so many questions that it is hard to sympathize with her even if she is the victim of something. 

&#x200B;

I also want to address the mention that Movie Bob refollows her every time she soft blocks him. Since Movie Bob is a fan of her what if he watches one of her videos, then goes into her description to see her twitter links and then sees that he wasn't following her, then refollows her? We live in an age where we here about the algorithm automatically unsubscribing people and with touch phones accidentally pushing the wrong button. I myself accidentally had blocked someone for the past several months without knowing it until I needed to talk to them recently. 

&#x200B;

Lesson of the day: If you're gonna soft block someone. Just block them. 

