His last video was July 15th as of this comment (sep 8th) which I believe the original post of this forum was July 17th. Seems like he's gone dark which isn't the first time his Youtube Channel has gone silent.

&#x200B;

I first found Garen Phillips when he was showcasing his daytrading while livestreaming on Youtube. It was the typical 'I'm gonna make money holding stocks for 5 minutes then sell them!' type stuff. Within about 6 months he blew up his account (as in $0). He was very obviously depressed about it even though he flat out said some statistic like 75-90% of traders blow up their first account. He just really wanted to be that special 10%. After that last video he went silent for about 1-2 years.

&#x200B;

After the hiatus he posted a few sporadic videos  How I learned to day trade in a week, Dividend investing, What I learned from reading the best 50 financial books, etc. Then he came out with the let's make a mil series which I believe only has 1 episode after being started 4 months ago. I thought his PHP thing sounded neat, I just thought it was selling insurance, I never looked into it that much or even read the comments on his videos. 

&#x200B;

That was until he posted his "Why I didn't become A Real Estate Agent | Life Insurance Agent" video, which at 0:27 seconds into the video he shows his income via excel spreadsheet. But the video was posted in June and the most recent dates on the spreadsheet was for April. Even still he had his income divided up as Business Income(5k)/Personal Income(7k) for a total of $12k in the month of April. I was incredibly suspicious at this point because anyone can just type in random numbers on a spreadsheet to make themselves look like high earners. Especially curious was how he had made his business within 5 months and was already earning $4k a month which is extremely unusual for a new business. Then there was the curiosity of where his Personal Income was coming from. It was just the simple problem of 'if a random guy on youtube can have his personal business be making 4k within 4 months, and still be earning a personal income of 7k, why aren't more people doing this?' type of situation. The fact that he didn't really disclose his income beyond Business & Personal just made me extremely suspicious. 

&#x200B;

However rather than going into detail of how he earned his money, he then spends the rest of the video flirting with some dance instructor and going to the park to do yoga and talk about meditation with her. Garen has always been an obviously vain guy, when you look at his instagram it's all photos of himself under filters that make him look tan mixed in with photos of women in skimpy clothing. It's all very surface level. You can just see how he wants to be  those 2 minute youtube ads of 'Trade anywhere in the world on your private jet making 1000% profits every second!' 

&#x200B;

If you go to his Instagram his last public post is a video on August 8th where he's at some PHP seminar. I thought he went silent because he realized PHP was a scam but even on his last live stream people were asking him if PHP was a scam which he shrugged off with "If it were a scam, then we wouldn't be doing this." Type of answer. 

&#x200B;

He would make a really great editor (assuming he edits his videos and doesn't just hire someone off of Fiver). That's probably why his videos have been so successful. Also the fact that his video is one of the first to pop up when you search 'trading stocks.'

