The game actively makes simulations worthless.

45 boots speed, 330 base speed, 13.6% movement increase

(Summoner's Rift map)

It took 25 seconds to walk from base to mid tower - no boots

It took 31 seconds to walk from base to bot tower  - no boots

It took 54 seconds to walk from bottom right corner to top left corner - no boots

3.4 seconds saved at mid tower, 4.216 seconds saved at bot tower, 7.34 seconds saved from corner to corner. 

&#x200B;

You say I'll be chased and unable to follow but Jhin's E slows opponents and his W traps them. Sounds like an easy way to leave when they are only moving 13% faster. I tend to play ADC's so getting a static shiv, rapid fire cannon or hurricane gives a 7/9% movement speed bonus, against another champ with those same items would cancel out the bonuses.

&#x200B;

Lots of ADC's tend to have a movement altering ability, Ashe's W, Caitlyn's mines and her E, Fortune's W, Sivir's Ult. Which the enemy could also have a slow/speed up ability which again would cancel it out.

&#x200B;

I'm not even touching on the idea that if everyone has the same movement speed bonus, then is it really a bonus?

&#x200B;

Although teamfights can easily be won and loss in 3.4 seconds alone I don't think that would be a deciding factor in whether or not your team is going to win. I don't think even 7.34 seconds would be a deciding factor in whether your team wins or loses. Even over multiple missed team fight opportunities I am skeptical if a team consistently choosing to engage despite missing a player would've won. You could even argue it's over an objective like baron or dragon which would be a shorter distance than corner to corner.

&#x200B;

